# VitaNet UI Design Rules

The approved redesign in `docs/VitaNet App Redesign.pdf` (56 frames, 390x844) is the
source of truth for every screen, dialog and sheet. Match it exactly; where these
notes and the PDF disagree, the PDF wins.

## Build with the shared kits
- Patient app: `lib/shared/widgets/vn_kit.dart` (`VnPalette`, `VnText`, `VnCard`,
  `VnButton`, `VnOutlineButton`, `VnChip`, `VnTextField`, `VnIconButton`, `VnDialog`, `VnSheet`).
- Hospital portal: `lib/features/admin/widgets/staff_ui.dart` and `portal_common.dart`.
- Take colors from `VnPalette.of(context)` / `AppColors`; never hardcode hex in screens.

## Redesign conventions
- Canvas `#F8FAFC`, white cards with a 1px `#E2E8F0` border, brand teal `#0F766E`,
  critical red for urgent states. Dark mode via the palette, never hand-picked colors.
- Headings: Plus Jakarta Sans, w700-w800, tight tracking. Body: Inter 13-15px.
- Radii as drawn: ~16-20px cards and inputs, 14px icon buttons, full pills for
  filter chips, allergy chips and recent searches, 28px top corners on sheets.
- Photos: use real clinical photography from `assets/images/photos` that fits the
  screen's job (people, care settings, the actual medicine). No stock gradients,
  no placeholder icons where the design shows a photo.
- Tinted icon tiles (rounded squares, soft brand/accent wash) are used where the PDF
  shows them; don't invent extra badges, overlay labels or feature checklists.

## Engineering rules
- A TextField inside a styled container must use a borderless, unfilled, dense
  InputDecoration so no inner box renders.
- Don't dispose a dialog's or sheet's TextEditingController right after
  `showDialog`/`showModalBottomSheet` returns; the exit animation still uses it.
- Keep screens responsive: the phone layout matches the PDF; wider layouts may add
  a side panel but keep the same content and copy.
